From 0420edc6e5f5eb64e65ca1bc30b5976e104d627c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ramesh Goswami <ramesh@listenfirstmedia.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:45:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] v0.5.0: bulk CSV/XLSX upload with tolerant headers and
 budgeted batching

- bulk.py: parse .xlsx/.csv (delimiter sniffing, BOM/latin-1 fallback, legend
  blocks above the header). Header aliasing so client sheets work untouched:
  Talent Name/Title/Full Name -> name, Title Category -> role, Sr. No. -> row_id.
  Role synonyms mapped; an unrecognised role is DROPPED with a warning, never
  guessed, since a wrong hint pushes the resolver at the wrong person.
- Header DETECTION is strict, header MAPPING is loose. A title cell like
  'Talent list for Q3' contains 'talent' and was being read as the header row.
- run_batch works to a wall-clock budget and returns unattempted rows, because
  ~5-10s per name against a 120s gunicorn timeout cannot finish a long sheet.
- template.py: fill-in workbook - Instructions, Input (6 examples incl. a
  Devanagari name, role dropdown, yellow input cells), Reference.
- app.py: /api/bulk/validate (parse only, no upstream cost), /api/bulk,
  /api/bulk/export, /api/template.xlsx, /api/template.csv. 4MB upload cap.
- UI: tabbed single/bulk, drag-drop, header-mapping preview, per-decision
  counts, results grid, Excel/CSV download.
- Fixed alias registration bug: keys held underscores while lookup normalised
  to spaces, so every underscored alias (row_id, active_year) silently missed.

256/256 tests pass across four suites. No credentials in any file.
